  "definition": "MAE is the unchanged val/<operator>_mae from the shared validation step, first per structure then averaged equally across structures; H uses the paper entry-weighted contribution diagnostic; historical within-structure S/D diagnostic reductions are preserved. RMSE, maximum, p95, p99 and R2 pool every observed shift-resolved sparse reference element across all validation structures, including both directed reverse entries and excluding padding/unobserved entries and prediction-only support. Predictions use physical envelope units and 0.5*(M + M.transpose().conjugate()) with reverse-edge alignment. H is converted from Hartree to eV; S and D retain native dimensionless units. For paper_restricted_total, the native spin=0 reference D is multiplied by two to restore the historical parser's documented spin-summed convention; this is a fixed provenance choice, not fitted rescaling. R2 = 1 - pooled SSE / sum(abs(reference - pooled_reference_mean)^2); R2 is null for a constant reference. mae_elementwise_pooled is an additional diagnostic, not the paper MAE. Percentiles are exact NumPy linear quantiles via in-place selection on a float64 temporary memory map; no histogram approximation or full validation tensor is used.",
